messages:
Maya: quick sync — I'm drafting a tiny addition to the docs style guide about pronouns + acronyms in examples. Goals: 1) use gender-neutral pronouns by default (they/them) in prose and examples, 2) always expand acronyms on first use (e.g., 'JSON (JavaScript Object Notation)'), 3) keep product and API names in Title Case (Redwood Inference, Redwood API), and 4) add a lint rule suggestion for automated checks. Thoughts? @Sam @Alex

Sam: +1 on gender-neutral pronouns. Only ask: when using 'they' in code comments, do we prefer it over explicit names?

Maya: prefer 'they' in prose and comments. For sample code where clarity matters, use short neutral names (e.g., `user`, `client`) or `alice/bob` only in protocol examples.

Jin: for acronyms — good call. Also propose a short exception list for brand abbreviations (e.g., 'SLA' can remain uppercase without expansion if it's common in the page). Might be worth adding that to the glossary.

Alex: I can open a tiny PR and add the rules + a few before/after examples. Will include a small Docs lint config snippet. Planning to branch from `docs/terminology-guidelines` and push today.

Maya: thanks. Example snippets to include (copy into PR):
```
// Bad
// The user set his API key in the dashboard.
// Good
// The user set their API key in the dashboard.

// Acronym bad
// Use JSON to structure the payload.
// Acronym good
// Use JSON (JavaScript Object Notation) to structure the payload.
```

Sam: tiny nit: for possessives, "the user's" vs "the user set their" — both ok, but keep voice consistent across a doc. Might add a one-line rule about keeping singular vs possessive forms consistent in a page.

Alex: noted — will add a doc-level checklist item: "Ensure pronoun/possessive consistency."

Docs Bot: PR created — https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/452 (Maya, Alex). CI: docs-lint running. :eyes:

Maya: awesome. Action items: Alex to finish PR with examples and lint rule; Jin to propose glossary exception list; Sam to scan a couple of high-traffic pages for regressions. I'll follow up with a tiny email to PX and support to let them know the wording update.

Alex: on it, will tag reviewers @Maya @Sam when ready.

Sam: thanks — happy to review.

Jin: will draft exception list and post here by EOD.

Maya: perfect. Closing the thread — feel free to ping if you need wording help. :thumbsup:
